// Idempotency-Key: replay cache for writes. Claim the key by inserting a
// pending row (unique PK = the lock); a racing/repeated duplicate resolves to
// 409 (in-flight) or a byte-identical replay (complete), never a double-run.
// Claims are BOUND TO A PRINCIPAL: on any collision the principal comparison
// runs FIRST — before the stale-pending takeover and before the replay branch
// — so a foreign caller can neither read a victim's cached body nor take over
// its abandoned claim. Unauthenticated requests carrying the header are
// rejected (400) unless the route is an explicitly opted-in PUBLIC action;
// opted-in routes get DEDUPE-ONLY semantics (duplicate ⇒ 409 reference, the
// cached body is NEVER served to a second caller).
